##### Di-jet Imbalance

Modification of the jet structure due to the medium induced gluon radiation is a much stronger effect than higher order gluon radiation which can happen also in p+p collisions and this makes the \(R_{\rm AA}\) so interesting quantity. However the size of the effect is dependent on the distance the jet has traveled in the medium. By triggering on the most energetic jet in the event one biases the selection towards the least modified jets. There is a high probability that the second (away-side) jet has interacted with the medium and has been thus significantly modified. Jet asymmetry \(A_{\rm J}\) (Eq. 3.15) should be therefore sensitive to the modification of the jets due to the presence of the QGP.

