Figure 8.3: TPC charged track multiplicity as a function of BBC coincidence rate. (a) No pile up reduction. (b) Additional event selection condition: \(|\rm{zVPD}-\rm{zTPC}|<4\) cm and only tracks with DCA\(<1\) cm accepted. (c) Same as (b) plus for each track a corresponding hit either in the BEMC or TOF is required.

The reconstructed jet spectra are corrected for the detector effects via unfolding in a similar way as in the case of Au+Au analysis. The correlated systematic uncertainty is quite large and is driven by the tracking efficiency uncertainty.

The ratio of the unfolded spectra and PYTHIA 6.426 Perugia 0 spectrum is plotted on Fig. 8.5. A cut on \(p_{\rm T}^{\rm lead}>5\) GeV/\(c\) was applied both in the numerator and the denominator. The p+p spectrum is in a decent agreement with the PYTHIA spectrum, taking into account the systematic errors. Thus the PYTHIA spectrum is validated as a resonable baseline for the \(R_{\rm AA}\) measurement discussed in the following section.

